      <activity id="7f4f6164-1a34-5d43-9072-95ad68ba62b2" activityNameId="b49ca484-b678-5c05-9022-4a22179145e9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Formaldehyde, production mix, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Formaldehyde, production mix, at plant
The processes that are used to produce formaldehyde from methanol are described in this inventory. These processes also produce steam, which carries part of the total environmental burdens. The process "oxidation of methanol" is a multi-output process;
UUID: cc69be77-6d77-3b80-b750-d870a31630e1
cradle-to-gate, including all precursors, ancillary materials and transports
Location: RER
Technology: represents a current cross-section of actual plants in Europe
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: see technology 
Extrapolations: see technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cc69be77-6d77-3b80-b750-d870a31630e1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
